#!/usr/bin/env perl
# PODNAME: robocop
# ABSTRACT: OCP robocop controller (in-cluster worker management)

use strict;
use warnings;
use FindBin;
use lib "$FindBin::Bin/../lib";
use OCP::Robocop;

# Run robocop controller
my $robocop = OCP::Robocop->new;
$robocop->run;

__END__

=head1 NAME

robocop - OCP Kubernetes controller for worker management

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    # Run robocop controller (inside K8s cluster)
    robocop

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Robocop is the in-cluster controller that manages worker nodes automatically.

B<Security Model:>

1. Waits for robo-ssh key injection (requires admin approval via PIN2)
2. Stores key in memory only (never on disk!)
3. Creates CRIU checkpoint in /dev/shm (tmpfs, RAM)
4. Watches Node and NodePool CRDs
5. Provisions workers using robo-key
6. CANNOT access control planes (robo-key not authorized!)

This script is the entry point for the robocop Deployment in Kubernetes.

=head1 ENVIRONMENT

=over 4

=item B<CHECKPOINT_DIR>

Directory for CRIU checkpoints (default: /dev/shm/robocop)

=back

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<OCP::Robocop>

=cut
